{"diagnosis": "Fetch progress signal max_addr stuck at 0x00000000 with TRAP: no progress vs expected sequential advance through 256-word NOP mem; tohost FAIL 0xdead confirms zero fetch. CONE_SLICE is empty so trace wins. Root cause in excerpt at picorv32.v:1450 `do_waitirq <= 1` forces wait-for-IRQ stall every cycle, blocking decode/fetch; default must be 0 like surrounding decoder_pseudo_trigger/trace_valid defaults.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -1446,7 +1446,7 @@
 		decoder_trigger <= mem_do_rinst && mem_done;
 		decoder_trigger_q <= decoder_trigger;
 		decoder_pseudo_trigger <= 0;
 		decoder_pseudo_trigger_q <= decoder_pseudo_trigger;
-		do_waitirq <= 1;
+		do_waitirq <= 0;

 		trace_valid <= 0;
", "expected": "tohost PASS (was FAIL 0xdead), TRAP: no progress cleared, max_addr != 0x00000000 with fetch progress"}

